<AdminDocument title="Privacy Policy" description="How the administrative services collect and use your data">
    <h2>Privacy Policy</h2>

    <p>Last updated July 19, 2026</p>

    <h3>Overview</h3>
    <p>
        This privacy policy governs your use of the "Diversifying the Violin Curriculum for Private Teaching" website
        administrative services, accessible at:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>kilmer.nrnnet.xyz/admin,</li>
        <li>www.kilmer.nrnnet.xyz/admin,</li>
        <li>kilmer.nrnnet.xyz/_emdash/admin,</li>
        <li>www.kilmer.nrnnet.xyz/_emdash/admin, and</li>
        <li>staging-spot-kilmerviolin.nrnnet.workers.dev.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        This policy outlines what information we collect when you use the administrative services, how we use that
        information, and how we protect your privacy.
    </p>

    <h3>Information We Collect and How We Use It</h3>
    <p>
        When you access this site, we may collect information and track your use of the service in accordance with this
        privacy policy. We use information we collect to provide the service, to improve the service, and to ensure the
        service's security. When you visit the administrative services, we collect data to:
    </p>
    <ol>
        <li>Provide the service requested;</li>
        <li>Improve the service's functionality; and</li>
        <li>Ensure the service's security and availability.</li>
    </ol>

    <p>When you visit the administrative services, we may collect:</p>
    <ol>
        <li>
            Information you provide directly to us, such as (but not limited to):
            <ul>
                <li>Data you enter into the database;</li>
                <li>Lookup and searches you request from the service;</li>
                <li>Files you upload to the service;</li>
                <li>Login and contact information, such as your email; and</li>
                <li>Any other information you choose to provide through the service.</li>
            </ul>
        </li>
        <li>
            Information about your requesting browser and device, such as (but not limited to):
            <ul>
                <li>your IP address;</li>
                <li>your approximated geolocation;</li>
                <li>any browser cookies you choose to transmit;</li>
                <li>your user agent;</li>
            </ul>
        </li>
        <li>
            Information about your interactions with the service, such as:
            <ul>
                <li>the date and time of your requests;</li>
                <li>the specific service features you use; and</li>
                <li>any errors you encounter.</li>
            </ul>
        </li>
    </ol>

    <p>
        Information you provide directly to us is maintained indefinitely until you or another user requests its
        deletion. Data you provide and save onto the database is accessible by any authenticated user and may be
        included on public-facing pages. After deleted, the data may still be recoverable through Cloudflare D1 Time
        Travel for seven days by an administrator.
    </p>

    <p>
        Information about your requesting browser and device originates from Cloudflare Workers Observability and is
        retained for no more than seven days. Data from Cloudflare Workers Observability is used to improve the service
        and ensure its security and availability.
    </p>

    <p>
        Information about your interactions with the service also originate from Cloudflare Workers Observability and is
        retained for no more than seven days. Data about your interactions with the service is used to improve the
        service and ensure its security and availability.
    </p>

    <h3>Data Sharing and Security</h3>
    <p>
        We do not sell or share your information, including with third parties. We only collect and use data to provide
        this web service and to produce the public website.
    </p>

    <p>
        As an administrator, you will authenticate through Cloudflare Access. Access offers authentication
        using Email OTP and Google Single-Sign-On. By logging onto the service, you agree to Cloudflare's Privacy Policy,
        accessible at{" "}
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy</a
        >, and Google's Privacy Policy, accessible at{" "}
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >policies.google.com/privacy</a
        >.
    </p>

    <p>
        We use industry-standard security measures to protect the information we collect. This includes authentication
        using Cloudflare Access, encryption of data in transit and at rest, and multiple layers of security and
        redundancy to protect against data loss and unauthorized access. However, no system is completely secure, and we
        cannot guarantee the security of your information.
    </p>

    <h3>Cookies</h3>
    <p>
        When you visit the administrative services, Cloudflare may set cookies on your browser. These are set in
        accordance with Cloudflare's Privacy Policy and generally are set to provide authentication and authorization.
    </p>

    <h3>Contact Us</h3>
    <p>
        For all inquiries related to this privacy policy, contact the system administrator at{" "}
        <a href="mailto:kilmer@mwmsc.net">kilmer@mwmsc.net</a>.
    </p>
</AdminDocument>
